WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.310
Hype for the third entry into the John Wick
franchise has been steadily building over

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.410
the past few months, and excitement is only
going to grow now that the first reviews for

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.160
the film are in.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.500
The minute studio Lionsgate lifted the restriction
on reviews for John Wick: Chapter 3 – Parabellum,

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.440
critics quickly published their thoughts on
the Chad Stahelski -directed actioner.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.560
Reviews for John Wick: Chapter 3 – Parabellum
are glowing, helping prove that the John Wick

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.620
movie series continues to outdo itself where
other follow-up films fall flat.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:33.340
JoBlo's JimmyO gave Parabellum a perfect score,
praising the film for its inventive action

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.460
sequences and its heart-pounding plot, which
sees our titular assassin John Wick, played

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.400
by Keanu Reeves, trying to outrun those who
want the $14 million bounty on his head after

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.760
he killed a member of the international criminal
group the High Table in John Wick: Chapter

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.260
2.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.440
JimmyO writes:

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.660
"This third chapter is one of the most thrilling
flicks you'll find in theatres so far this

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.340
year, and somehow, they've found new ways
to bring men to their knees.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.440
The violence is near operatic, capping off
one of the best damn trilogies ever made […] It's

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:06.960
impossible to remember the last trilogy that
worked nearly as well as John Wick - aside

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.660
from perhaps Lord of the Rings, which is timeless.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.900
The third film continues to build the mythology
in the most satisfying of ways.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.060
It's a ferociously fast and immensely breathtaking
adrenaline ride of a flick!"

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.440
He added that John Wick: Chapter 3 – Parabellum
is, quote, "certainly in the running for one

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.760
of the best films of the year."

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.420
Robert Kojder of Flickering Myth was another
critic who stamped Parabellum with an impeccable

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.680
five out of five stars.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.860
He said of the film,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.799
"Put it this way, if George Miller's Mad Max:
Fury Road was the legendary filmmaker showing

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.420
youngsters how it's done, this is Chad Stahelski
firing back.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.880
Much like Chapter 2, Chapter 3 leaves you
begging for more.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.240
At this point, the John Wick movies are becoming
a new drug, so go get your fix.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:51.360
Prepare for more than war, prepare for constant,
exhilarating anarchy."

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:56.080
Chris Nashawaty of Entertainment Weekly had
wonderful words for Parabellum, particularly

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.360
how its action scenes, which are a mainstay
in the franchise, were choreographed.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:05.540
He also applauded actresses Halle Berry, who
plays an assassin named Sofia, and Anjelica

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:10.340
Huston, who portrays the Director of the High
Table, for giving performances that add, quote,

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.200
"a jolt of unexpected emotional weight" to
the movie.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.580
Nashawaty made his feelings about John Wick:
Chapter 3 abundantly clear in the final lines

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.300
of his review:

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:22.140
"I don't mean to give the impression that
John Wick 3 is anything grander than a gorgeously

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.880
choreographed, gratuitously violent action
movie.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:29.640
But as gorgeously choreographed, gratuitously
violent action movies go, it's high art."

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:35.180
Uproxx's Mike Ryan exalted Parabellum as the
best film in the franchise, due in large part

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:39.980
to how the movie expands on the series' existing
world and mythology without ever feeling bogged

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.900
down or less fun than its predecessors.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.520
"Like John Wick himself, this third chapter
feels like a lean, mean, fighting machine

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:51.260
- and, yes, it's the best film of the franchise
so far, even surpassing the first film.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.020
There are moments in John Wick: Chapter 3
– Parabellum where I thought to myself,

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.680
'Well, I've never seen that before.'"

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.080
Chris Evangelista of Slashfilm called Parabellum

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:06.170
"...a bone-cracking, horse-kicking, dog-biting,
book-smashing, ax-throwing action masterpiece."

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.620
while Fresh Fiction's Courtney Howard described
it as

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:13.080
"...an eye-popping, jaw-dropping, show-stopping
next chapter that extends the world-building

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:17.280
beautifully, whilst assigning meaningful resonance
to the character-driven action."

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:22.720
USA Today's Brian Truitt was largely impressed
with John Wick: Chapter 3 – Parabellum,

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.300
calling it a "solid continuation of the killer
franchise that makes James Bond look about

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:32.159
as hardcore as Peppa Pig," though he did admit
that the supporting characters - like Laurence

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:37.010
Fishburne's Bowery King, Asia Kate Dillon's
The Adjudicator, and the big bad Tick Tock

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:40.580
Man, played by Jason Mantzoukas - were a little
underdeveloped.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.160
He also wrote that the final act was a bit
messy.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:48.340
"This third movie brings both the operatic
action and intriguing exposition, though misses

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:54.300
the greatness of Chapter 2 because of a convoluted
last act and underdeveloped supporting characters.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.220
[...] In the Wick-verse, a bloody action usually
leads to much more trouble later.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:03.060
As long as that's at the heart of this series,
a pretty good Chapter 3 still equals insanely

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.200
explosive, two-fisted exhilaration."

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:09.920
Alissa Wilkinson of Vox also brought up the
point of John Wick: Chapter 3 – Parabellum

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.620
lacking some, quote, "narrative intelligence,"
but argued that whatever the film is missing

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.919
in that regard, it makes up for in style and
visuals.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.359
"Should the John Wick universe have a more
coherent mythology?

00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:23.689
Should it come up with some kind of a point
it wants to make?

00:04:23.689 --> 00:04:27.280
Should it, in other words, try to become a
smart series of movies at some point?

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.280
No, I don't think so."

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.240
"Oh."

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.340
"Parabellum is just as satisfying as its predecessors,
and not just because of the Tick-Tock Man.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.220
It is not, to be clear, a smart or wise movie
- it's just a really fun one."

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.720
Of course, no film is entirely perfect.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.020
Though the overwhelming majority of critics
applauded for John Wick: Chapter 3 so hard

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.020
that their hands went numb, there was one
who wasn't completely blown away.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:59.580
Variety critic Andrew Barker felt that Parabellum
was difficult to watch in that it features

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.720
so much violence and doesn't let up.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.240
"What do you need?"

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.240
"Guns.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.160
Lots of guns."

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.939
He did, however, give kudos to director Chad
Stahelski and the entire creative team for

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:13.240
making something so visually masterful.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.179
"On a level of pure craft, then, John Wick
3 is unquestionably great action filmmaking

00:05:18.179 --> 00:05:22.860
- certainly the most technically accomplished
of the series thus far [...] But as masterfully

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:28.149
executed as the action is, watching two-plus
hours of mayhem without any palpable dramatic

00:05:28.149 --> 00:05:34.700
stakes, or nuance, or any emotion at all save
bloodlust offers undeniably diminishing returns."

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:39.360
By and large, the reviews speak for themselves:
people are picking up what John Wick is putting

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.840
down in Chapter 3.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:46.080
If the film's critical success thus far translates
into big bucks at the box office, perhaps

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.620
Parabellum won't end up being the end of the
John Wick series.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.919
After all, according to Uproxx's Mike Ryan,
Parabellum "doesn't really try to play coy

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.080
about a fourth movie."

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:59.220
Decide for yourself if John Wick: Chapter
3 – Parabellum gets your blood pumping when

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.160
the film hits theaters May 17.

